{
  "produced_by": "voice_agent",
  "source_narration_script": "You're not unhappy at work. You're just stuck. Every small change you can think of makes things a little worse, so you stay put. Picture a lobster in a trap. To get out, it has to crawl deeper into the cage, back toward the center, before it can reach the opening. But every instinct pulls it toward the light. So it stays trapped by its own good sense, because the way out is the one direction that feels wrong. That's you on a hill in thick fog. The ground falls away in every direction, so it feels like the top. But a far higher peak could be hidden across the valley. You'll never find it unless you walk downhill. A worse move today can be the price of a better peak tomorrow. What's the step back you keep refusing?",
  "alignment_ratio": 1.0,
